            {
                "entry_id": "02b90af5-2d38-338f-8767-5f438e23abd3",
                "word": "caddy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "56b5ba88-3d32-42b0-9e27-4778e96fa622",
                        "entry_id": "02b90af5-2d38-338f-8767-5f438e23abd3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "caddies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "15918126-59f2-3a18-b1e5-c9f668a5da42",
                        "entry_id": "02b90af5-2d38-338f-8767-5f438e23abd3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative spelling of caddie (“a person hired to assist a golfer by carrying their golf clubs and providing advice”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative",
                            "attributive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5314a1c7-37e1-4247-9859-fee769ab8201",
                                "sense_id": "15918126-59f2-3a18-b1e5-c9f668a5da42",
                                "text": "Caddy, pass me my five iron."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3c3e70b-b6ae-42c4-a6c2-da62d5f69068",
                                "sense_id": "15918126-59f2-3a18-b1e5-c9f668a5da42",
                                "text": "As caddy I had to carry the clubs, for there are four varieties almost everyone used, and some used more. Besides doing this, the caddy has to keep score of the number of strokes used, and watch and find each ball."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b60bb1ab-24b1-41c5-bc26-ec9ccf3f8757",
                                "sense_id": "15918126-59f2-3a18-b1e5-c9f668a5da42",
                                "text": "Then Carter Chapman picked out his putter, stepped confidently up to the ball, sighted once along the ground, and made his stroke. The ball rolled straight as a die toward the caddy who was holding the flag, and tinkled into the cup for a birdie three!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "113eda3b-5028-306f-b644-adadce2fdff0",
                "word": "Caddy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "726b37ab-1b73-46d5-a44b-fba52c4b12bd",
                        "entry_id": "113eda3b-5028-306f-b644-adadce2fdff0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Caddies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5f542b89-b481-38f7-9d60-f4b18ebec90e",
                        "entry_id": "113eda3b-5028-306f-b644-adadce2fdff0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Cadillac car."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9c35130-858f-486a-b3e1-781ebaccaecb",
                                "sense_id": "5f542b89-b481-38f7-9d60-f4b18ebec90e",
                                "text": "She pulled up in a shiny black Caddy at six o'clock."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d68e2dda-66bb-40de-b049-6ecf62ec8cd0",
                                "sense_id": "5f542b89-b481-38f7-9d60-f4b18ebec90e",
                                "text": "All those ones live in those great big piecrust mock-Two-door houses with His and Hers Caddies parked out by the hydrangea bushes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee7cd6ff-dc2f-4e83-b7dc-8aebe8203cad",
                                "sense_id": "5f542b89-b481-38f7-9d60-f4b18ebec90e",
                                "text": "He's driving a ten-year old^([sic]) lime-green Caddy with a trunk full of golf clubs and one suitcase. We got a license number."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6fa4abd2-bad9-4587-a9b3-d02e9608fd93",
                                "sense_id": "5f542b89-b481-38f7-9d60-f4b18ebec90e",
                                "text": "So Dave backed his car in beside the Caddy, his eyes on the side door of the bar, no one having come out for a while."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
